  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1235 PM MST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nUpper level analysis shows upper trough axis centered from the \nUpper Midwest through the Southern Plains. Further upstream, water\nvapor imagery shows closed upper low moving onshore across northern\nCA and OR/WA. Diffuse surface high pressure over the northern Rockies\ninto Northern Plains with brisk NW surface flow across the forecast\narea. Lingering low clouds across south-central SD will erode this\nafternoon with widespread sunshine today. Winds will diminish through\nthe day as the surface low pulls eastward. Western upper low is \nforecast to eject into the Southern Plains Wednesday into Thursday,\nalthough precipitation will remain east the area. Generally dry \nweather will persist through the week with seasonable temperatures.\nDry clipper system will push through the Northern Plains Friday \ninto Saturday, although wind potential has diminished considerably\nfrom previous model runs. Western ridge will build Sunday into \nearly next week. Temperatures are trending 5-15F warmer than \nnormal Sunday through Tuesday. Ensemble guidance keeps the area \ndry through at least mid-week next week before more active western\nflow returns by end of next week, although there are no major \nprecipitation signals thus far.",
